        <p>UNDOUBTED CONSUMPTION CURED.</p>
        <p>Night Sweats, the most certain symptom of Consumption, had • already commenced. Patient saved by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>[From the Glamorgan Free Press.]</p>
        <p>Mr. JOHN HOLLAND, Of 25, William-street, Cilynydcl, near Pontypridd, Wales, was brought back to health Npri vigour under difficult circum- stances. An athletic broad bhouldered man, standing six feet in his socks, Mr. Holland is twenty- six yftats of ago and single. Two y( ais ago he was attacked by influenza, and from that time his egperienoe was one of great suffering. For eighteen months he was too ill to do any work. His die- ease was undoub- tedly Consumption, sought on by an</p>
        <p>decline went on far six months. I am weaver, accl I bad to leave my work, for I was beginning to feel that I couldn't hat much longer. I had wasted away to skin and bone, and another siEt,2r of mine had to do my housework for me. At the end of the six months I could scarcely walk, and at intervals I had spent two or three days at a time in bed. Accompany- ing my helpless state of weakness was an incessant, racking cough, which shook me terrib'y."</p>
        <p>"A —doctor Whom I consulted told me he could do me no good, so I had given myself up, and my friends, too thought I was rap.dly followin my sister's fate. That has turned out to he an unwise prognostication, for when at last I had become so weak that I could with difficulty get about, a friend of mine told me to try Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People. I told her I was tired of trying things ; however,when my hug band came home I suggested the matter to him, and h went out and bought two boxes or the pills. Well, after I had taken half a box I felt better already, and when I had taken three boxes I actually went back to the mill. "My fellow-workers never thought I should go there again' but when I did. I felt as though I could cry with joy. I kept On taking the pills, and altogether I took five boxes."</p>
        <p>Mra. Dardis did not now show any signs of following in the fomtsteps of her sister. Consumption, although hereditary, in her case has been cured.</p>
        <p>A LADY DECLARED DYING OF CONSUMPTION.</p>
        <p>Curei by Dr. Williams' Pink Pins.</p>
        <p>[From the Sheffield Independent.]</p>
        <p>" I am thirty-four years old," said Mrs. Barnet, of 18, Bing-street, Masbro', near Sheffletd, to a reporter on the staff of the Sheffield Weekly Ind epen- ri dent curing a con- versation, and at the time I was married, some fif- teen years ago en- joyed good health, After the birth of my Eecond child, nine years ago, however, my health began to fail. My appetite fell away, and so did my fl,sh, and I lost s'reog,th, andenergy as well. I grew steadily worse every month. In vain</p>
