      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-03-24_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <head>Effected the Cure.</head>
        <p>Effected the Cure.</p>
        <p>[From the Holntfirth Express.</p>
        <p>At Hade Edge, Holmfirth, near Hudderfield, stands a clump of cottages known as Flowery Field. A Holm- firth Express r _porter found there Mr. Eli Smith, a locomotive driver, and his son Fred, a boy of fifteen years. Fred had been an ailing child sinca he was 18 months old a doctor saw the boy when the parents resided at Burn- ley, and said he feared Consump- tion. After the Smiths removed to.Holmfirth, another doctor, was called in to attend the boy, and he confirmed the opinion of his brother medical man ; naturally /1 the parents were ‘-•‘\ / alarmed. They '`\\ / determined to do all possible for their s-n, and their attention be- newspaper article to the many cures I effected by Dr. 'Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, they accordingly purdhased a supply. The pills were admin- istered regularly, and an improvement was gradually observed.</p>
        <p>The parents became convinced that this was the one remedy that would "build up "their boy's health, for whereas, formerly, the boy's heart seemed to heave at the sight of food, and drops of perspiration would appear on his cheek, now this is changed, and the lad can appreciate good food. The left lung affectim that the doctor spoke of now gives the boy no trouble, and the delicate invalid is giving place to a sturdy youth. The father spoke highly of the Dr. Williams Medicine Co. in courteously giving advice by post, and said in return the Company were at liberty to publish the above particulars, as the boy was "steadily gaining health, strength, and weight, and the great benefit he had received they attributed solely to Dr. Williams' Pink Pills." They said they had been encouraged by hearing the much•talked of cure effected by the pills in the case of a farmer's dau.,h.'er at Holmfirth, who now enjoys the pink of health.</p>
        <p>Mr. Geerge Craven (a friend of Mr. Smith) said "I have known the bay two years, and could not but notice the change for the better in his appearance." Dr. Williams' Pink Pl!a are not Lire other medicine, and their effects are permanent. They act directly on the blood, and thus it is that they are so famous for the cure not. only of consumption, but also of ansetnia, rheumatism, paralysis, and 8,:,. Vitus' Dance. They are now obtainable of all chemists, and Enna Dr. Williams' dicine Company, 46, Holborn-viaduct, London, at. 2s. 9d. a box, or six boxes for 131. 91., but are c:enuiue only with full name, Dr. Williams' Pink Pills far Pale People.</p>
