        <p>little boy in Surrey.</p>
        <p>KENT.</p>
        <p>The superiority of Scott's Emulsion over other forms of cothliver oil could not be any more clearly demonstrated than in the case of a little child in Surrey, who, owing to a severe illnef s of the mother, had to be brought up by baud. The father cf the child, Mr. H. Kent,tells in a few words the history of the case. He says: "267, Remany-road, "W. Norwood, Surrey,</p>
        <p>" dctober..2ist. 1898.</p>
        <p>"Dear Sirs,—lt gives me great pleasure to tell you how very beneficial Scott's Emulsion has been to ay little son. Be was a strong child when he was born, but owing to the misfortune of his mother having a severe illness, we were obli:ed to bring him up by hand, and in consequence he did not thrive, but got very weak. Our doctor ordered cod-liver oil for him, but he was too weak to digest it, and could not retain it on his stomach. Seeing, however, that Scott's Emulsion contained cod-liver oil, I determined to try the preparation, and finding that it agreed with my boy I continued is use, and have proved it to be a substantial food, for he has progressed in health and strength, and is altogether a different child since taking Scott's Emul- sion. I must say I think it a very valuable</p>
        <p>ow Scott's Emulsion linnefite4 a</p>
        <p>Preparation. and one . that cannot be toe widely known, for by its use I believe very many children could be mvfol much suffering. I shalt recommend Scott's Emulsion whenever I have an. opportunity.</p>
        <p>"In grai'itude, believe me, yours very sincerely, (Signed) H. ICErrr." The foregoing was a typical case trr the Scott's Emulsion treatment. People make the mistake every day of giving to-children forms of cod-liver oil which they cannot digest, and all of this diffi- culty could be avoided if they would give them Scott's Emulsion instead. This preparaton com- bines cod-liver oil, hypophosphites and glycerine, each of these substances being standard t•medies, endorsed by the medical prof,ssim. The beauty of Scott's Emulsion is in combining these remedial agents into a perfect and palatable emulsion, which makes each of its ingredients more p tent than if emnloyed alone. S3ott's emulsion is the best remedy in the world for children, as you yourself will ad- mit if you try it.</p>
        <p>You can obtain a samplo of Scott's Emulsion by sending threepgice to cover postace tl Scott and Bowne, Limited, Manufacturing Chemists, 95,Great Saffron Hill. London, E.C., and mentioning this .p3per. All chemists szll Sect's Emulsion.</p>
