      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-03-24_WidnesExaminer_art0049" n="art0049">
        <head>ACADEMY-STRHET HALL.</head>
        <p>ACADEMY-STRHET HALL.</p>
        <p>On Sunday, Mrs. J. A. Johnson, of Roo.hdale, paid her first visit to the local Spiritualists Society. In the afternoon the speaker gave an address on "The gift of God is eternal life." In the evening the sub- ject Iva:, "How our loved ones have broken through the partition dividing the two world's " After each address a number of clairvoyant descriptions of those who have crossed the border were given, and on Monday Mrs. Johnson, after a few remarks, de- voted the rest of the evening to clairvoyance and psychometry.</p>
        <p>CYCLES.—Prerniers, £lO lOs ; Excelslors. 212 Os Os. New Rapids £l5 108 Od. Sole Agent J. S. GARLAND, LA.DIES BRST GLACE BOOTS min SHOES UNDER THE CLOCK, BRIDGE-STBEET.—Advt.</p>
