        <p>IkCCIDENT AT A WIDNES WORM,</p>
        <p>Daniel SpNocer, aged 17, ra3iding at 21, Midwood- street, while following his employment ac the Electric Copper Wok. on Saturday, suffered ssvero injuries to his right hand. Three ein4ers were amputated. through his hand being cruitsed between• some rollers. He was removed to the Accident flos&amp;al, where his injuries were attended to. TEMPERANCE CONCERT AT WIDNES.</p>
        <p>Oa Monday evening a concert was elven in the Lacey- street Schools, Widnes in aid of tn 3 Tamper woe Society. There was a fair attendance, and Mr. B. Browne occu- pied the chair. Th 3 artistes were the Misses Hague, mime, and Eiarrison, and Messrs. A. Shingler, J Stnich, Bowen, H. Wilkins us. and 1344geridee, and the Milton Quartet. Miss F. Wailing accompanied the soloists. Daring the evening selections on the phoeogr soh were given by Mr. L. Hargreaves, assi4tel by Me. Patten, which added considerably to the egilyment of the proceedings.</p>
