      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-03-24_WidnesExaminer_art0051" n="art0051">
        <head>BRASS BAND CONTEST.</head>
        <p>BRASS BAND CONTEST.</p>
        <p>On Saturday evening, the Widnes Borough Jubilee Brass Band held their first annual quartette C3Rt.sr. in the Drill Hall, Widnes. There was a good audience. Fourteen quartette parties competed, and the test pieoe was their own selevion from the Wright and Rounds 2nd and 9th selections far quartettes. Mr. W. Rirnoaer, of Southport, officiated as judge, and his adjudications were as tOIIOWEI :—(1), Widnes St. Mary's, conductor. J. J. Brady; (2), Crooke, conductor, J. Fairhurst ; (3), Sutton Band, conductor, J. Appleton ; (4), Gossages' Soap Works ; (5). Etrlestown Viaduct. Subsequent to the judge's decisions being anneunced, Mrs. Alfred Kenyon presented the winners with prizes.</p>
