        <p>A PICKPOCKET NE&amp;TLY CAUGHT</p>
        <p>At the Warriogton Borough Police Court, on Monday morning, bef ire Mr Birchall (in toe chair) and other magistrates, Henry Reberta, a working man, described as lodging at the 'British Wwirkman public-house, Horse- market-street, wis charged with stealing a purse from the dress pocket o Mre. Ryder.—Superintendent slorsi- ghan state 1 that Mrs. Ryder got on the 'oaa at the Cemetry on Saturday of ernr oa. and she had in her pocket a p use containing 4P. The prisoner at next to her, but when Scotland-road had been reached she found that her purse was missing. The prisorPr hur- riedly left the 'bus, and susoectio cr he had stolen it the called to him "to stop." He refuted to do so, ani she got off the 'bus and !Allowed him alo sg Sootland-road, when he threw the piirire to the grliind and ran off. In- format'on was given to a policeman who was near at hand (P.C. Johnscri), and the man was taken into cus- tody. Superintendent M maghan added teat for two hours the prisoner was ioitering about the Cemet3ry,and he was seen to get on and off slveral 'bases. The sum of 2s. was found in one of his pockets.—The Clerk said that numerous complaints had been received about to conduct of pickpockets on 'buses.—The Chairman : Yes, and we mast put a stop to it, The prisoner will have to go to gaol for a mmth with hard labour.</p>
