        <p>R. E. KEEBLE, Parkside Asylum, Macclesfield:—"l have much pleasure lin bearing favourable testimony to the</p>
        <p>'merits of AreoColl •</p>
        <p>"I am an at-</p>
        <p>tendant in the sick ward of the above asylum, and my duties call for constant watchfulness, care and attention in attending to the wants of the patients, entailing great strain on both mind and body.</p>
        <p>"Some time ago I found I was losing flesh, and at the end of the day was quite weary and tired. My appetite began to fail, and I often suffered from headache and nausea, especially after meals. Seeing an advertisement of ,D;./.cocog I determined to try it, which I did, and found it very nourishing and sustaining, the result being that I am able to perform my duties without the least fatigue or weariness, My appetite has been restored, and I am no longer sub- ject to headache or nausea.</p>
        <p>"I recommended my fellow-attendants in the ward to try Mama, and they (seeing the change it had made in me) took my advice, and now drink nothing else, and always speak of the great benefit they have derived from its use.</p>
        <p>" I shall always feel grateful to Dr. Tibbles' Vi- Cocoa for having been the means of restoring my health and energy. I can confidently recommend We,rfirria to anyone who is in want of a tonic, also to those whose work calls for great exertion and en- durance.</p>
        <p>" You are at liberty to make what use you like of</p>
        <p>this testimonial,"</p>
