        <p>render a good account of themselves. WIDNES v. FLEE ['WOOD. At Widnes. Widnes, who payed ten A. Team men,' had a runaway victory, tries being scored by Brown, Lomax (thre,i), O'Brien, Fostr (two), ald Leyshon ; whilst Dsmosey scored for Fieetweod. The goals were , plan tid by Aspev an.l Thomas. Final score : Widees, six a 041,1 arid 12 tries (48 points) ; FLetwood, one try (three p,inas). DRAW FOR THE SECOND ROUND. v Wirriegton widues v Dewsbury Leigh v Runcera S. li..lens v Merecambe C astleford v Briehluse Raagers Normanton v H etiecir Swinton v Fluntlet Batley v York L9E115 V Vrig,'Sll Hull v Milhm Brougiron Rangers v Hull Kingston Rovers Ellen] v Bowling Bradford v Rochdale Hornets Huddersfield v fleekmondwike Out wood Church v Led. Parish Church Salford v Weraeth Oa the ground of the first-nam'A. REFEREES FOR THE SECOND ROUND. The following appointments have heee made br local matches in toe secon I round of the (nip competition next SA:urdavi—BrougaGon Rangers v Hull Kingston Rovers, referee A Brawn (Brighouse Ranger,). touch judges J T KSOWIPS (VVerringtou) and P "wham (Oldham) ; v Warrington, referee J Priestley (Broughton Ran- gers), touch judges R Abbey (S7oiroort) and J Underwood (Wigan) ; Swinton v Hueslet, referee T H Marshall (Bradforl), touch jul4es R U Moore (Oldham), and W Civgg (Stockport) ; St. Hel•-ns v Morecambe, re- feree H Eagles (Salford), touch jicli,es A Willwork (Leigh) aad T Barnes (Warrington) ; Widnes • Dews- bury, referee T H Eagland (Huddersfield), touch judges .W Jones (Runcora) and W Nevins (Warrington) ; Sal- Ford v Werneth, referee F 'Turner (Warrington), touch judges J M`Gowan (Brill:x(41On Raegers) and J Edwards (St. Helens ); Laigh v Run:torn, reteree W MiCutcheen (Oldham), touch judges S Williams (Salfori) and J Graham (it. Helens). MEETING OF THE LANCASHIRE SENIOR COMPErnioN. At a meeting of the eominitte ia Lancaster last night, Mr. J. H. Smith (Widnes) in the chair, Bolts of Werneth, was suspended up to and including April 15th for charging. The case of Warrington claiming Allen, who, Warrington St. Mary's contend, is a member of their club, was adjourned for the proluction of the St. Mary's minute b)ale to show the date when Allen joined them. J. James was grars'ed crxrusgion to play with Broughton Rangers. Taylor, of St. Heleas, for kicking, waa suspended for one week.</p>
