        <p>thrORTANT ANNOUNCEA ENT. THE COMING VISIT OF . • • , LORD GEORGE, THE ORIGINAL SANGER'S, THE LARGEST AND MOST FAMOUS lIJPP,iDRAMATIC, SPECTACULAR, AND V• ARIETY CIRCUS IN THE WORLD. NOW KNOWN AS THE QUEEN'S OWN CIRCUS, BY GRANT OF HER MAJESTY. The same Lord George. the Original Sanger, that received the Royal Command to bring his present travelling Circus to Balm ,ral Castle, on the 17th of June of last year, for Her Majesty's pleasure and enj Jyment, the Queen sitting in the Royal Box three hours and seven minutes, from the com- mencement to the close of the Royal Progtaname. TuE QUEEN'S OWN WORD 3 :—' The very best perform - anon of its kind I have ever seen." THREE GIGANTIC CIRCUSES. HIPPODROME AND DOUBLE FREE MENAGERIE. 430 HORSES AND PONIES 460. The present Tour has been one series of triumphant and unparallelled successes. The entire British public taken by storm. The GREATEST EXHIBITION THAT EVER TRAVEL- LED HER MAJESTY'S DOMINION'S, WARRINGTON BLUE COAT SCHOOL GROUND, • THURSDAY, MARCH 30Ts, TWO PERFORMANCES IT 2.30 and 7.30. The great feature this year is the production of an elaborate NAVAL AND MILITARY SPECTACLE, entitled "WITH KITCHENER TO KHARTOUM" Representing the recent victories at Atbara. Omdurman. and Khartoum, produced on a scale of magnificence and mounted with an amount of completeness never before equalled. The hoisting of the colours of the United Empire and Egypt over the Palace of Khartoum; the Flight of the" Kalipha, leaving behind the wives of the Harem on the wey ; Camel Corps in pursuit. Then the mimic, snul-stirring, representation of the most famous fight of modern times, in which the terrific engines of destruction, the latest products of our naval armaments, are engaged in a terrible battle with the gunboats of the Kalipha ; Victory of the British Fleet, manned by British tars and commended by British Officers; Total destruction of the Kalipha's boats—blown up and sunk. , This production has entailed an outlay of many Thousands of Pounds. In reading this announcement the public will receive the statements as facts,and not, what' is too often the case, appearing only upon paper. SEE THE GREAT FLEET IN YOUR STREETS. Each Boat from 60 to 60 feet in length. The Spectacle is a masterpiece of production, specially invented, arranged and organised by Lord t:-; eorge the Original Sanger, the Oldest Proprietor in the World and the Monarch of all Showmen. UndouUtedly the Pre-eminent Amusement Enterprise of the British Nation. The GIGANTIC MENAGERIE and SUPERB NEW AVIARY. consisting of Will Animals, Birds Beasts and Reptiles, will ho OPEN FREE OF CHARGE from 10 to 4 daily, and will form part of the GREAT STREET PAGEANT AT 1 O'CLOCK; Worth a journey of 100 miles to witness. TWELVE MONSTER ELEPHANTS, including '• H.R.H." the 'identical animal upon which our popular Prince rode when on tour in India. TWO FLOCKS OF CAMELS AND DROMEDARIES. ELEVEN REAL GUNBOATS, being exact replicas of those used in the recent NAVAL ENGAGEMENT WHICH TERMINATED IN LORD KITCHENER'S VICTORY AT KHARTOUM. TICE WORLD'S OLDEST AND GREATEST SHOWMAN, LORD GEORGE, THE ORIGINAL SANGER. THE QUEEN'S OWN CIRCUS. • Two Performances at 2-30 and 7-30. Wet or Fine. The Public Never Dif.appointed. Prices of Admission, from Sixpence to Half-a-Guinea. NO CONNECTION WITH ANY OTHER SANGER'S CIRCUS.</p>
