        <p>PETER COTTON. ROPE AND TWINE MANCE ACTUREIL Backing, Canvas, Stack-corners, Netting Curled-hair, Oil Sheets, Isc., &amp;c. TENTS and MARQUEES for Sale or Hire. SPORTS, PICNICS, eo., fitted complete. 6, CHESTER'S-YARD, WIN WICK-STREET, WARRINGTON. B OROUGII OF WARRINGTON. WARRINGTON CORPORATION BILL, POLL OF OWNERS AND RATEPAYERS. WHEREAS A PUBLIC MEETING of the Owners and Ratepayers of the Borough of Warrington was dely held on Wednesday,the 18th day of January, 899. in the Gymnasium Pelmyra-square, in the said Borough, in pursuance of the Act of the 35th and 35th Victoria, cap. 91, intituled " an At to authorize the Application of Funds of Municipal Corpora- tions and other governing bodies in certain cases.' AND WHEREAS at the said Meeting held at the time and place aforesaid. I, as Chairman of such Meeting, and in com- pliance with the St&amp; ute proposed the following Resolution— That this Meeting, as representing the Owners and Rate- payers of the Borough of Warrington. do, pursuant to the provisions of the Act of the 36th and 36th Victoria, chapter 91, intituled •• An Aet to authorizs the Applica- tion of Funds of Municipal Corporations and other governing bodies in certain cases," approve of and con- sent to the following resolations of the Council of the said Borough, passed at their Meeting held in the Town Hall, Warrington, on the 3rd day of January, 1899 nem That ..own Council do prcmote a Bill in the next " Session of Parliament for the construction of additional Waterworks and the Improvement of the Borough "of Warrington, and for other purposes." 'That the costs and expenses in relation to promoting "such Bill be charged upon the Borough Rate or other " Bates and Funds under the control of the Council as . 'the Council may decide." AND WHEREAS the said resolution, on being put, was carried, whereupon demand was made that sueh question should be decidect,by a Poll of owners and Ratepayers. AND WHEREAS such Poll o the Owners and Ratepayers of the Borough of Warrington has been duly taken by rue,iu manner by law required under the provis ons of the Public Health Act, 1875, by meani of Voting Papers. Now I hereby give notice, certify, and declare that the result of such poll is as follows, viz : The number of Votes given in favour of the said re- solution is 9,419 The number of Votes given against the said resolu- tion is Majority in favour AND I HEREBY FURTHER GIVE NOTICE, certify and declare that as the result of the said Poll the said resolution has been duly passed and adopted. Dated the Bth day of March, 1899. JOHN EDWARD WRIGHT, Mayor.</p>
