        <p>LATEST NEWS. FOOTB ALL-LIVERPOOL y, SHEFFIELD UNITED. The re-played semi-final tie between Liverpool and Sheffield United took place at Bolton yesterday. Liver- pool led by 1 goal to ml at half time, but the final score WAS 4 goals each. . DEATH OF A FAMOUS MA.NUFACrURE R. Intimation was received by telegraph in Bir,ningham yesterday morning that Mr. Richard Cadbury, the head of the firm of Cadbury and Company, tne wtllknosx chocolate and cocoa manufacturers, had died at Jcru- salem. The deceased gentleman was on a tour through the Holy Land with trrlnbers of the family. THE WINDSOR HOTEL FIRE. NEW YORE, THURSDAY. What are believed to be the remains of three more victims of the Windsor Hotel fire were taken out yester- day evening. This brings the total number of deaths up to 18. LATEST LOCAL WEA.THER FORM IST. The following forecast of the weather for the ensuing twenty-four hours in the north-west of England (in- cluding Macnester,Liverpool,and HolvhPa I) was issued at the Mlteorological Offiec at three o'clock yesterday afternoon:— North-easterly winds, light or moderate, Fair gener- ally. ANOTHER FATAL POWDER EXPLOSION. BRESLAU, THURSDAY. According to a telegram from Reichenstein an ex. plosion occurred at Fodmersdorf at ten o'clock 3 esterday morning in one of the sheds of a powder manufactory belonging to Kommerzeinrath Gucttler. The shed was completely demolisbed,and two workmen who were em- ployed in it at the time were killed.</p>
